    "raw_text": "Anderson, Policy Committee to Highlight How Local Organizations Help Families Cope with Rising Costs\nSeptember 30, 2026\nWHAT\n: \tHouse Republican Policy Committee Chairman David H. Rowe (R-Snyder/Union/Mifflin/Juniata), Rep. Marc Anderson (R-York), and other lawmakers will host a hearing titled “Neighbors Helping Neighbors: Examining the Ways Local Organizations are Helping their Communities Deal with Rising Costs” to highlight the important work community organizations are doing to help families meet their basic needs amid rising costs.\nWHO\n: \tTestifiers will include Eric Saunders, executive director, New Hope Ministries; Thad Sales, pastor, Calvary Methodist Church; Rodney Carberry, commander, Dillsburg Legion; Pastor Matthew Castillo, founder, Believers Earling Learning Center; Dean Van Zanardi, director, Veterans Lake Fishing; and Shirley Fortunato, member, Calvary Methodist Church.\nWHEN\n: \tThursday, Oct. 1, at 10 a.m.\nWHERE\n: \tNew Hope Ministries, 99 West Church St., Dillsburg, PA 17019\nLIVESTREAM\n: Barring any technical difficulties, the hearing will be streamed at\nfacebook.com/policycmte\nand\ntiktok.com/@policy_committee\n.\nMedia contact: Nancy Nilson, nnilson@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
